      "category": "other",
      "components": ["R4", "R11", "R12"],
      "pins": ["R4.1", "R4.2", "R11.1", "R11.2", "R12.1", "R12.2"],
      "nets": ["/PWM2_C1", "/PWM2_C2", "Net-(J8-Pin_3)", "GND"],
      "observed": "R11 and R12 are 0-ohm jumpers connected between the M5Stack bus pins (/PWM2_C1, /PWM2_C2) and GND. R4 is a 1k resistor connected between J8 pin 3 (Net-(J8-Pin_3)) and GND. There is no net named /PWM2 in the netlist.",
      "expected": "R11 and R12 should connect /PWM2_C1 and /PWM2_C2 to a common /PWM2 net, and R4 should be a 1k series resistor from /PWM2 to J8 pin 3, as specified for the PWM2 channel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) in net GND; (node (ref \"R11\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) in net /PWM2_C1; (node (ref \"R12\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) in net GND; (node (ref \"R12\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) in net /PWM2_C2; (node (ref \"R4\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) in net GND; (node (ref \"R4\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) in net Net-(J8-Pin_3)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R9–R12 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | Select which M5Stack bus pin (pin 19/21 for ch.1, pin 20/22 for ch.2) supplies PWM1/PWM2"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The PWM2 channel is non-functional. If R11 or R12 are populated, they short the corresponding M5Stack bus GPIO pins to ground, potentially damaging the M5Stack. R4 pulls the J8 signal pin to ground, preventing PWM2 or the serial bus from driving it correctly.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a miswiring in the PWM2 channel: R11/R12 connect the M5Stack bus pins to GND instead of /PWM2, and R4 connects J8 pin 3 to GND instead of acting as a series resistor from /PWM2. This breaks PWM2 and can short bus pins to ground."
}

